      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1i1irr9'
    '|b||So the rent decides whether the yard makes money. It has nothing to say about what one more boat costs.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:f96hxd'
    '|a||Rent that never moves is a feature of the short run. Given a few years, the yard can build a bigger shed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6400
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||And every shed size gets its own U. A bigger shed costs more rent, but it builds a lot of boats cheaply.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1g5crvk'
    '|a||For each number of boats, Kai picks, out of every shed size he could build, the one with the lowest curve there. Trace that lowest edge, and you get the long-run average cost, LRAC.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1nzvujf'
    '|b||It wraps around the U''s from below, like an envelope.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1nn921c'
    '|a||Where it falls, there are economies of scale: double the shed, the tools and the crew, and you get more than double the boats.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:14rzl46'
    '|a||Partly that''s geometry. Double every side of a tank, and it takes four times the steel but holds eight times as much.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:a4s2r3'
    '|b||And partly it''s people. In a big yard one builder can do nothing but hulls, another nothing but rigging, and each gets very good at it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1u75kv7'
    '|b||Your turn: sort these. Cheaper or dearer as the yard grows? Sort each card.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:enxij9'
    '|a||Where the envelope turns up, diseconomies of scale: more layers of managers, slower decisions, and nobody quite sure who is doing what.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9920
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||So average cost falls when the yard shares out what''s fixed or grows everything together, and rises when something can''t keep up.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:14jfwh'
    '|b||But the Model T got cheaper partly for another reason, one that none of these curves can show.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||In 1936 an aircraft engineer, Theodore Wright, tracked how many hours of work each new plane took.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:104gao9'
    '|a||Every time the total number of planes ever built doubled, the labour for each new one fell by about a fifth. Here is that rule as an ideal curve, illustrative.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1j0lciv'
    '|b||So cost depends not just on how much you make this month, but on how much you have ever made. That''s a learning curve.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6760
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:121t80o'
    '|a||Solar panels have followed the same rule: about twenty percent cheaper for each doubling of all the panels ever installed. A whole drawcast tells that story.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:9rl81o'
    '|b||Is that really learning, though? Or just bigger factories and cheaper silicon?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4600
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:nokhur'
    '|a||Gregory Nemet took solar costs apart in 2006. Bigger plants, more efficient cells and cheaper silicon did most of the work, and learning by doing explains them only weakly.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:bbqhre'
    '|a||So how sure are we? That bigger operations make each unit cheaper in many industries: mostly agreed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:pj0tyl'
    '|b||That average cost turns up again for giants: contested. Since the 1950s many studies find it flattens out instead, more an L than a U. And how much of a learning curve is really learning is contested too.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 14400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:gcbi72'
    '|a||Three new cases. A half-empty ferry takes on one more foot passenger. What does that passenger add to the ferry''s costs?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:xatajm'
    '|a||Almost nothing: the crossing, the fuel and the crew are paid for anyway, so the marginal cost is near zero.':
